  "ingredients": [
    "1/2 teaspoon chipotle seasoning",
    "1/2 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "1/2 teaspoon onion powder",
    "1/2 teaspoon ground coriander",
    "1/2 teaspoon smoked paprika",
    "1/4 teaspoon cumin",
    "1/4 teaspoon dried oregano",
    "1/8 teaspoon cayenne pepper",
    "1 tablespoon olive oil",
    "32 ounce bone-in, skin-on chicken thighs",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Mix the spice blend using all of the ingredients listed (except for the olive oil, chicken, salt, and pepper).",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/crispy-chipotle-chicken-thighs/#wprm-recipe-51221-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8343.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Start to de-bone the chicken thighs. Using kitchen shears, cut a direct line above the bone going through the thigh.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/crispy-chipotle-chicken-thighs/#wprm-recipe-51221-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8369.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using the scissors, cut around the bone until you can lift it out of the chicken. Make sure to get as close to the bone as possible – you don’t want too much wasted meat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/crispy-chipotle-chicken-thighs/#wprm-recipe-51221-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8365.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cut around the end that is still attached and remove the bone from the chicken. Repeat for all the chicken thighs. Cut off the excess skin as needed.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/crispy-chipotle-chicken-thighs/#wprm-recipe-51221-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8379.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lay the chicken skin-side down on top of paper towels. Season with salt and pepper, then with your seasonings mix. Liberally coat the chicken meat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/crispy-chipotle-chicken-thighs/#wprm-recipe-51221-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8381.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using a meat hammer, lightly pound the chicken to get a consistent width. You want this to cook evenly.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/crispy-chipotle-chicken-thighs/#wprm-recipe-51221-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8393.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Flip the chicken over so that the skin is now facing up. Coat with salt and pepper, then cut each thigh in half.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/crispy-chipotle-chicken-thighs/#wprm-recipe-51221-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8398.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat olive oil in a cast iron skillet over medium-high heat on the stove.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/crispy-chipotle-chicken-thighs/#wprm-recipe-51221-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_84065.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the pan is hot, add chicken thighs skin-side down into the pan. Let this cook for 8-10 minutes. Do this in two batches.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/crispy-chipotle-chicken-thighs/#wprm-recipe-51221-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8415.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cover your pan with a grease catcher screen to keep the excess grease from going everywhere.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/crispy-chipotle-chicken-thighs/#wprm-recipe-51221-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8421.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "After 8-10 minutes, flip the chicken over and cook on the other side for 2-4 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/crispy-chipotle-chicken-thighs/#wprm-recipe-51221-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8429.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Optional: Wilt some spinach down in the remaining chicken fat and serve with lemon to squeeze lightly over the chicken thighs.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/crispy-chipotle-chicken-thighs/#wprm-recipe-51221-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
